{"name":"Protégé Bronze","hex":"#66543e","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"protégé","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A person who is guided and supported by an older and more experienced person (a protector or mentor)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/prot%C3%A9g%C3%A9"},{"term":"bronze","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A naturally occurring or man-made alloy of copper, usually in combination with tin, but also with one or more other metals.","A reddish-brown colour, the colour of bronze."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Made of bronze metal.","Having a reddish-brown colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bronze"}],"entries":[{"title":"Mentorship","blocks":[{"text":"Mentorship is the patronage, influence, guidance, or direction given by a mentor. A mentor is someone who teaches or gives help and advice to a less experienced and often younger person. In an organizational setting, a mentor influences the personal and professional growth of a mentee. Most traditional mentorships involve having senior employees mentor more junior employees, but mentors do not necessarily have to be more senior than the people they mentor. What matters is that mentors have experience that others can learn from."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e4/US_Army_52782_Mentoring_the_next_generation.jpg/330px-US_Army_52782_Mentoring_the_next_generation.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mentorship","wikidata":"Q967647"},{"title":"Bronze","blocks":[{"text":"Bronze is an alloy consisting primarily of copper, commonly with about 12–12.5% tin and often with the addition of other metals and sometimes non-metals or metalloids. These additions produce a range of alloys some of which are harder than copper alone or have other useful properties, such as strength, ductility, or machinability."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/Bull%27s_head_ornament_for_a_lyre_MET_DP260070.jpg/330px-Bull%27s_head_ornament_for_a_lyre_MET_DP260070.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bronze","wikidata":"Q34095"},{"title":"Bronze (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Bronze is a metallic brown color which resembles the metal alloy bronze. An archaic term for it was aeneous."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c9/Bronze_medal_for_bravery_%28Austria-Hungary%29.png/330px-Bronze_medal_for_bravery_%28Austria-Hungary%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bronze_(color)","wikidata":"Q2778382"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/39/Age_Teaching_Youth.jpg/500px-Age_Teaching_Youth.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/39/Age_Teaching_Youth.jpg/500px-Age_Teaching_Youth.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"William Blake's \"Age Teaching Youth\", a Romantic image of mentorship[15]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAge_Teaching_Youth.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/Senior_editor_mentoring_junior_editor.jpg/500px-Senior_editor_mentoring_junior_editor.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/Senior_editor_mentoring_junior_editor.jpg/1280px-Senior_editor_mentoring_junior_editor.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/Senior_editor_mentoring_junior_editor.jpg/500px-Senior_editor_mentoring_junior_editor.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt"